WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.844
The SiT dataset makes several contributions.

00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:08.691
It provides large-scale real-world pedestrian
trajectories gathered as a robot navigated

00:00:08.771 --> 00:00:12.013
densely populated indoor and outdoor environments,

00:00:12.093 --> 00:00:16.731
from building interiors and campuses to crosswalks
and public walkways.

00:00:16.811 --> 00:00:20.917
It lets researchers build prediction models using
rich context,

00:00:20.997 --> 00:00:26.033
including appearance features, the robot's
ego-motion, and semantic map data.

00:00:26.113 --> 00:00:33.276
It achieves precise time synchronization between
all sensor modalities using a centralized triggering method,

00:00:33.356 --> 00:00:35.668
which makes sensor fusion practical.

00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:40.651
It supplies multi-layered semantic maps for both
indoor and outdoor scenes.

00:00:40.731 --> 00:00:46.099
And it offers a curated benchmark covering 3D
detection, 3D multi-object tracking,

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:51.681
trajectory prediction, and an end-to-end task from
perception to motion forecasting,

00:00:51.761 --> 00:00:53.940
with everything released publicly.
